  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**This is the even version of the Grid Construction Problem. Both are worth 50 points each.**\n\nYou are given an **even** integer NNN.\n\nNow your task is to construct a grid AAA containing NNN rows and NNN columns such that :\n\n\nFor every i,j(1≤i,j≤N)i,j(1 \\le i,j \\le N)i,j(1≤i,j≤N) 1≤Ai,j≤N1 \\le A_{i,j} \\le N1≤Ai,j​≤N have to be satisfied.\nFor every x(1≤x≤N)x(1 \\le x \\le N)x(1≤x≤N), xxx appears **exactly** NNN times in AAA.\nLet S1S_1S1​ be the sum of elements in the diagonal from top-left to bottom-right and S2S_2S2​ be the sum of elements in the diagonal from top-right to bottom-left, Then :\n\nSum of all elements in every 222 adjacent rows has to be equal to S1+S2S_1 + S_2S1​+S2​.\nSum of all elements in every 222 adjacent columns has to be equal to S1+S2S_1 + S_2S1​+S2​.\n\n\nIt can be proven that at least one valid answer exists.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first and only line of input contains NNN - the dimension of the grid.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output NNN lines each containing NNN integers. The jjj-th integer in the iii-th line should represent Ai,jA_{i, j}Ai,j​ of the grid you constructed.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤301 \\le T \\le 301≤T≤30",
      "2≤N≤5002 \\le N \\le 5002≤N≤500",
      "NNN is even",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 500500500."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n2",
        "output": "1 2\n2 1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : Here, S1=2,S2=4S_1 = 2, S_2 = 4S1​=2,S2​=4. Further, every row and column also adds to 333. Thus, adjacent row(column) sum = 666 = S1+S2S_1 + S_2S1​+S2​. Hence, this grid is valid."
      }
    ]
  },
